# Vendure Server Patterns

Full guide: `apps/server/AGENTS.md`. Vendure docs (MDX): [developer-guide on GitHub](https://github.com/vendurehq/vendure/tree/master/docs/docs/guides/developer-guide). Scaffold with `npx vendure add -p <name>`.

## Plugin checklist

1. `@VendurePlugin({ imports: [PluginCommonModule], … })`
2. `entities`, `providers`, `shopApiExtensions` / `adminApiExtensions` as needed
3. Register in `vendure-config.ts`
4. Generate migration: `npx vendure migrate <plugin-name>`

## API layer (resolvers)

- Thin resolvers → delegate to services.
- Always `@Ctx() ctx: RequestContext` first arg; pass `ctx` to all service/connection calls.
- `@Allow(Permission.…)` on queries/mutations; `@Transaction()` on mutations.
- GraphQL SDL in `api/api-extensions.ts`; resolvers in `api/*.resolver.ts`.

## Service layer

- `@Injectable()` services with business logic.
- Inject `TransactionalConnection` and core services from `@vendure/core`.
- DB access: `this.connection.getRepository(ctx, Entity).findOne({ … })` — always pass `ctx`.
- Eager-load relations explicitly; use `EntityHydrator` when relations aren't guaranteed.

## Entities

- Extend `VendureEntity`; register in plugin `entities` array.
- `@EntityId()` for FK id columns; `@Money()` for prices.
- Custom fields: `configuration` callback + `types.ts` module augmentation + migration.

## Worker / jobs

- Lifecycle hooks run in server **and** worker — guard with `ProcessContext.isWorker`.
- Create job queues in `onModuleInit` / `onApplicationBootstrap`; reuse queue when enqueueing.
- Never pass raw `RequestContext` as job data — use `ctx.serialize()` or minimal fields to recreate context in the worker.

## Config / env

- Plugins do not read `process.env`; pass values via `Plugin.init()` from `vendure-config.ts`.
